<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil eases, demand steady.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil eases, demand steady.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.5066)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     37.50/37.80     24.89/25.08     38.20/38.50</p>
<p> BREMEN		37.50/37.80     24.89/25.08     38.20/38.50</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    37.60/38.00     24.95/25.22     38.50/38.80</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   38.20/38.60     25.35/25.62     39.00/39.30</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   38.40/38.70     25.48/25.68     39.10/39.40</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  39.40/39.70     26.15/26.35     40.00/40.40</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices slid back on Monday, pulled lower by weaker underlying futures. Buying volumes were steady on firm demand for heating oil from end-users. - London newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
